@startuml delivery-paths
!include state-machine-style.iuml
title Slop Machine | Delivery paths at a glance
caption All paths require checks and senior-agent approval of the exact code to publish.

state "Agent review approved\nChecks passed" as Ready
state DeliveryMode <<choice>>
state "Push branch + open PR\nVerify remote commit" as PR
state PRReviewMode <<choice>>
state "Await human review\nNo active run or slot" as Awaiting <<attention>>
state HumanDecision <<choice>>
state "Repair or reconcile\nRecheck + senior review" as Repair
state "Merge PR\nVerify target commit" as Merge
state "Direct-main gate\nExpected head + permission" as DirectGate
state "Fast-forward push main\nVerify remote head" as PushMain
state "Update task status\nJira Done if ticket linked" as Done
state "Complete\nCode + task status verified" as Complete <<success>>
state "Needs attention\nFinal rejection or blocked policy" as Attention <<attention>>

[*] --> Ready
Ready --> DeliveryMode : delivery mode from task specification
DeliveryMode --> PR : [pr_human or pr_automatic]
DeliveryMode --> DirectGate : [direct_main; no PR]
PR --> PRReviewMode : PR head verified
PRReviewMode --> Awaiting : [pr_human]
PRReviewMode --> Merge : [pr_automatic; host rules satisfied]
PRReviewMode --> Attention : [pr_automatic; host requires human]
Awaiting --> HumanDecision : authenticated PR/chat response\n/ start new run
HumanDecision --> Repair : [changes requested]
HumanDecision --> Merge : [approved; gates current]
HumanDecision --> Attention : [final rejection or ambiguity]
Repair --> Ready : new exact snapshot approved
DirectGate --> PushMain : [main unchanged; final snapshot approved]
DirectGate --> Repair : main or final snapshot changed
DirectGate --> Attention : permission or protection denied
Merge --> Done : merge verified
PushMain --> Done : main push verified
Done --> Complete : applicable task/ticket update verified
Complete --> [*]
Attention --> [*]

note right of PushMain
  No PR and no force push.
  Concurrent tasks serialize main integration.
end note
@enduml
